 "autotile": {
  "code": "scripts/assets/autotile.mjs exports autotileName(get, x, y, tileset) implementing all of this.",
  "dungeonWalls": "A \"#\" with floor directly south is a FACE: wall (wall_face_l / _r / _single when floor is west / east / both). Every other \"#\" is a wall TOP: call a neighbour \"open\" if it is floor or a face; then N+W open -> wall_inner_nw (likewise _ne, _sw, _se), S -> wall_cap, N -> wall_edge_n, E -> wall_edge_e, W -> wall_edge_w; only a diagonal open -> wall_corner_se / _sw / _ne / _nw; nothing open -> wall_top. Floor: wall to the north -> floor_shadow, wall to the west -> floor_shadow_w, wall only NW -> floor_shadow_corner. Rooms look best with north walls 2 thick (cap above the face).",
  "townWater": "For \"~\": land N+W -> water_nw (likewise _ne/_sw/_se), one side -> water_n/_s/_w/_e, land N+S -> water_river_h, land E+W -> water_river_v, land only diagonal -> water_inner_ne/_nw/_se/_sw, else water. Treat \",\" and \"=\" as water. In the dungeon \"~\" -> water_dungeon and \",\" -> water_shallow.",
  "houses": "An H/D block: bottom row is the wall (house_wall_l / house_wall / house_window / house_door / house_wall_r, or the stone_house_ set); the row above it is the low roof (house_roof_low_l / _low / house_roof_gable at the right end, or roof2_*); higher rows use house_roof_l / house_roof / house_roof_r. Houses look right 3 rows tall (2 roof + 1 wall).",
  "bridges": "\"=\" with water north or south -> bridge_h (crossing east-west), else bridge."
 }
}
